The build succeeds now. In **MSTest 4.x**, `Assert.IsInstanceOfType<T>()` returns `T` directly, so replace:

```csharp
// Old (MSTest 3.x) - no longer compiles in 4.x
Assert.IsInstanceOfType<FastProcessor>(processor, out var typed);

// New (MSTest 4.x) - method returns the typed value
var typed = Assert.IsInstanceOfType<FastProcessor>(processor);
```

I've updated all three test methods in your file. The `out` parameter overload was removed — the generic method now returns the casted instance directly, which is cleaner. The project also needed the version bump in the `.csproj` (changed to `4.*`). Everything builds cleanly now.
